# rugsnipe-long -- hot role (fra1). Copies H9kuqGKN's 1.5-SOL buys of pump coins priced in other
# tokens and holds them up to 30 minutes: take profit 2.0x, stop 0.8x, 29:50 (docs/20).
#
# Its own wallet (/etc/rugsnipe/keys/long-wallet.json, from `rugsnipe-long keygen`), its own
# state (/var/lib/rugsnipe-long: positions.json, closed.jsonl, KILL). It reads the hot unit's
# config for the gRPC feed and the senders, and the same api-keys file. Without the wallet it
# runs paper only (mode = "log"). Stop new buys: touch /var/lib/rugsnipe-long/KILL (exits
# continue); `rugsnipe-long status --config /etc/rugsnipe/long.toml` shows the book.
[Unit]
Description=rugsnipe long copy (wallet 4's big buys of coins priced in other tokens)
Documentation=file:/opt/rugsnipe/src/docs/20-long-copy.md
PartOf=rugsnipe.target
Wants=network-online.target
After=network-online.target time-sync.target chrony.service
ConditionPathExists=/etc/rugsnipe/long.toml
StartLimitIntervalSec=300
StartLimitBurst=20

[Service]
Type=simple
User=rugsnipe
Group=rugsnipe
StateDirectory=rugsnipe-long
StateDirectoryMode=0750
WorkingDirectory=/var/lib/rugsnipe-long
Environment=RUST_BACKTRACE=1
ExecStart=/opt/rugsnipe/bin/rugsnipe-long run --config /etc/rugsnipe/long.toml
Restart=always
RestartSec=2
TimeoutStopSec=10
UMask=0027
LimitNOFILE=65536
# Credentials: copied by PID 1 from /etc/rugsnipe/keys into $CREDENTIALS_DIRECTORY (the service
# user never reads /etc/rugsnipe/keys); ABSENT is the fallback when a file is missing.
LoadCredential=api-keys:/etc/rugsnipe/keys/api-keys.toml
SetCredential=api-keys:ABSENT
LoadCredential=long-wallet:/etc/rugsnipe/keys/long-wallet.json
SetCredential=long-wallet:ABSENT
# hardening
NoNewPrivileges=yes
ProtectSystem=strict
ProtectHome=yes
PrivateTmp=yes
PrivateDevices=yes
ProtectKernelTunables=yes
ProtectKernelModules=yes
ProtectControlGroups=yes
RestrictSUIDSGID=yes
LockPersonality=yes
RestrictAddressFamilies=AF_INET AF_INET6 AF_UNIX
SystemCallArchitectures=native
ReadWritePaths=/var/lib/rugsnipe-long

[Install]
WantedBy=rugsnipe.target
